I've described this solution with a rationale:

Generate 'junk'[1] items into monsters inventory and mark these and 
randomly some other items that monster carry as not usable. Probe would 
show these, they would be vulnerable to attacks but the monster wouldn't 
use them.

When monster picks up an item the item is discarded[2] or a timer is 
attached into it. After the timer goes off there is a chance depending 
on the monsters intelligence or some such that the item is marked as 
unusable. The length of the timer could be tied to a items utility 
value[3], which might depend on the monster also.

These unusable items represent those items that the monster has gathered 
but have forgotten that she even has. This nicely mimics those DOH's 
that we all have had when we look at the inventory disclosure after death.

[1] 'Junk' in a a sense that its utily to a monster that is only cannon 
fodder is nil.

[2] As an example: When a monster picks up an armor piece that isn't 
immediately used it should be dropped if heavy, or marked as soon to be 
forgotten. Same goes to heavy weapons.

[3] Non utility items still might have curiosity value and everything is 
interresting to a nymph[4] but one still forgets that they are there.

[4] Nymphs will carry anything but almost all is marked as unusable[5].

[5] This opens a little can of worms[6]: Should all monsters 
automatically know what items are?

[6] Just enough for some leisure fishing.

